{
  "subtype": "faceted_decomposition",
  "concept": "audience_praise_and_complaints",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "praise_type",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "Praise is one of the two named halves of the concept 'praise and complaints'. Capturing the type/aspect of praise expressed is a constitutive part-of the concept — it is an aspect OF the audience reaction, not an external predictor of it."
    },
    {
      "name": "complaint_type",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "Complaint is the other named half of the concept. Its type is a constitutive facet of audience_praise_and_complaints, decomposing the negative valence of the reaction."
    },
    {
      "name": "subject_target",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "The target of the praise/complaint (film, actor, director, screenplay, etc.) is an intrinsic aspect of the reaction itself — every praise or complaint is about something. It is meronymic (the 'what it is about' dimension), not an external cause or predictor."
    }
  ],
  "facet_columns": ["praise_type", "complaint_type", "subject_target"],
  "non_facet_columns": [],
  "mutual_exclusivity": 0.55,
  "exhaustiveness": 0.75,
  "rationale": "All three columns are genuine constitutive facets of the concept, decomposing valence (praise vs. complaint) and target. However mutual exclusivity is weakened: praise_type and complaint_type draw from largely the SAME underlying value vocabulary (acting_performance, screenplay_writing, cinematography_visuals, direction, character-related aspects), so the 'aspect' dimension is duplicated across the two valence columns; furthermore subject_target overlaps heavily with the *_type columns (e.g., performance_actor / director / screenplay in subject_target restate acting_performance / direction / screenplay_writing in the type columns), so the same content-aspect is captured twice under different names. Exhaustiveness is fairly good: the type columns cover the main quality dimensions (acting, writing, visuals, direction, pacing, technical, originality, emotional impact) and the target column adds the object dimension, together spanning valence × aspect × target. What is not cleanly separated is intensity/strength of sentiment, but the core constitutive aspects of what praise and complaints consist of are largely covered."
}

